NAME
    rssh - start a managed shell with the rsudo shell extension

SYNOPSIS
    rssh [<shell-argument> ...]

DESCRIPTION
    rssh starts the managed shell environment with the selected package-owned
    rsudo.lib.sh as the shell extension. The m-rsudo package must already be
    installed and selected through the current shell context.

    Before delegating to shell, rssh locates rsudo.lib.sh in the selected
    m-rsudo concrete's link/lib/sh view on PATH, exports that absolute path
    as m_SHELL_EXT, and installs an RSSH prompt in PS1. The prompt uses tput
    capabilities for terminal styling and shows the current user, host and
    working directory.

    All command-line arguments are forwarded unchanged to shell.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m rssh [arguments].

    m_SHELL_EXT
        Exported as the selected m-rsudo@<version>/link/lib/sh/rsudo.lib.sh
        pathname before shell startup.

    m_PKG_DIR
        Required package store root used to constrain extension lookup to
        installed m-rsudo package views.

    PATH
        Must include exactly one selected m-rsudo link/lib/sh view (repeating
        the same view is harmless). Other package versions are ambiguous.

    PS1
        Replaced with the RSSH prompt used by the managed shell session.

    SHELL
        Consumed by shell to select the shell executable. See the shell manual.

EXIT STATUS
    rssh delegates shell preparation, execution and resulting status to shell.
    Local pre-shell failures are:
        1   m environment missing
        2   m shell runtime unavailable
        3   package store root missing
        4   selected rsudo shell extension unavailable
        5   multiple different rsudo shell extensions selected
    Otherwise the launched shell status is propagated.

DEPENDENCIES
    rssh is an m-integrated command. It uses the m runtime roots and delegates
    to the shell facility. The selected shell session loads the package-owned
    rsudo.lib.sh through m_SHELL_EXT without requiring a legacy global copy.

SEE ALSO
